// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR E_FIELD_MODULE_PRIVATE
//
// std-hygiene (владелец, 2026-07-10): `Vec[T]` declares its `len`/`cap`/`data`
// fields `priv` (module-private, `collections.vec`) and the only public API is
// the `len()` method (Plan 124/D220 + Plan 160/D281 same-name field/method
// pattern, mirrors `Job` in `nova_tests/plan160`). A BARE (non-call) member
// access `raw.len` — no parens — used to silently compile from any importing
// module and read the raw private struct field directly: the checker's
// same-name-method fast path in `f3_check_member_ctx`
// (compiler-codegen/src/types/mod.rs) returned right after materializing the
// field's type for the non-call form, WITHOUT ever running the priv-field
// gate below it (that gate only guarded the plain-field branch, reached only
// when NO same-named method exists). Fixed by mirroring the priv-field check
// into the same-name-method non-call branch
// ([M-173-priv-field-samename-bypass]).
//
// Repro is the owner's exact finding: `ro n = raw.len`.

module neg.neg_vec_priv_field_bare_access
import std.collections.vec.{Vec}

fn bad_len(raw Vec[int]) -> int {
    ro n = raw.len
    n
}
